        "created_at": "2017-04-10T18:32:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Congratulations.</p><p>Mr. Chomps isn't newborn friendly. &nbsp;the fabric isn't going to hold up under beatings and slober and all the things a primary stuffed companion has to survive with newborns.</p><p>I wouldn't go with Mr. Chomps as a primary companion, not one to sleep with or drag around and chew on. &nbsp;It's not really unsafe or fragile, just not newborn -toddler friendly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
